It's modeled after the sun-managers mailing list and shares the same
policy.

In short, decstation-managers is an unmoderated list intended to
provide DECstation system administrators with a quick-turnaround
troubleshooting aid.  Answers to posters' questions are mailed
directly to them, where they are summarized and sent out to the list.
This keeps the number of messages to a minimum.  Discussion is very
strongly discouraged.

Systems that fall under the DECstation label currently are the 2100,
3100, and 5000 MIPS-based workstations running Ultrix.  VAXstations
and the larger RISC DECsystems are not valid topics of discussion
except in areas overlapping the DECstation realm.

